From b76364781db181574815910d11ad7a3f3e9a94ba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 07:36:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] soc: qcom: spm: use a raw lock for the MSM8226 L2 regmap

The shared APC path accesses this map while holding a raw lock with IRQs
disabled and may run on CPU0 through an IPI. On PREEMPT_RT fast_io alone
selects a sleeping spinlock for regmap-MMIO. Select the raw lock
explicitly so register callbacks cannot sleep in the caller's atomic
context.

The actual regmap lock-selection/callback model previously reproduced
the owner and PMIC parent failures. The separate PMIC parent fix is also
needed for that complete chain; physical RT and lockdep acceptance
remain open. Ported from qualified Codex fix
3621db8f609490bccee6296f9b5ff7720c255447. Implementation, changelog and
qualification used OpenAI Codex assistance.

Fixes: e3b7530c31dc ("soc: qcom: spm: initialize the MSM8226 L2 arbiter master")
---
 drivers/soc/qcom/spm.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/qcom/spm.c b/drivers/soc/qcom/spm.c
index 2b8150160dc..0bfa99fde0d 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/spm.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/spm.c
@@ -554,6 +554,7 @@ static const struct regmap_config spm_8226_l2_regmap_config = {
 	.reg_stride = 4,
 	.max_register = 0xffc,
 	.fast_io = true,
+	.use_raw_spinlock = true,
 	.rd_table = &spm_8226_l2_read_table,
 	.wr_table = &spm_8226_l2_write_table,
 };
